mfmediaengine: Autoplay, and present video in rendering mode (MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_PLAYBACK_HWND).

Photoshop 2027's "What's new" dialog (the UXP plugin com.adobe.photoshop.inAppMessaging) showed an empty grey box
where each card's video belongs. UXP's <video> creates its IMFMediaEngine in rendering mode: only
MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_CALLBACK and MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_PLAYBACK_HWND, no MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_FORMAT. Three gaps:

1. media_engine_create_video_renderer failed with "Output format was not specified", so the topology had no video
   branch. In rendering mode it now uses B8G8R8X8.
2. Wine never drew anything in rendering mode. A render thread now takes the frame due at the presentation clock
   from the frame sink and draws it into the playback window with StretchDIBits, aspect-fitted (HALFTONE). Size and
   stride come from the sink's current type; RGB with no stride is bottom-up, as for a DIB. The thread is joined in
   free_media_engine.
3. SetAutoPlay stored the flag but nothing used it, and UXP's <video autoplay> never calls Play(). As in the HTML
   media element, a paused engine with autoplay set now starts when its source has loaded.

Tests: tests/mf/mfautoplay.c (SetAutoPlay, no Play: before FAIL, never plays; after PASS) and tests/mf/mfhwnd.c
(rendering-mode playback into a window, counts lit pixels: before FAIL 0 pixels; after PASS 147371/147456).

